The GPU scales the full raw image to the preview, but the ordinary Bayer
statistics path sampled only a preview-sized rectangle at the raw image's
top-left corner. A 640x480 preview therefore metered a tiny, unrelated area
of the sensor. Unlike the CPU line path, DebayerEGL::process() passes the
complete raw buffer to SwStatsCpu and does not offset its origin.

Meter the whole input for ordinary Bayer, keeping the existing Quad Bayer
geometry intact. This fixes exposure/white balance without altering JPEG
brightness or overriding sensor controls behind libcamera's back.

--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
@@ -358,11 +358,12 @@
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * Don't pass x,y from window_ since process() already adjusts for it.
-	 * But crop the window to 2/3 of its width and height for speedup.
+	 * GPU output is scaled from the full raw image. process() passes that
+	 * whole buffer to the stats path, without applying window_'s offset.
+	 * A preview-sized window here would meter just the raw top-left corner.
 	 */
-	stats_->setWindow(quadBayer_ ? window_ : Rectangle(window_.size()));
+	stats_->setWindow(quadBayer_ ? window_ : Rectangle(inputCfg.size));
 
 	inputBufferCount_ = inputCfg.bufferCount;
 	outputBufferCount_ = outputCfg.bufferCount;
